556
00:34:55,550 --> 00:34:58,650
diagnosis, will be presented
by other colleagues.

557
00:34:58,990 --> 00:35:03,890
Anyway, initially, the
pathology of tuberculosis

558
00:35:03,890 --> 00:35:08,310
is related to granuloma
formation and acute

559
00:35:08,310 --> 00:35:11,150
pneumonia, which
subsequently becomes chronic.

560
00:35:11,290 --> 00:35:14,610
This stage is called
primary tuberculosis and

561
00:35:14,610 --> 00:35:17,370
occurs in previously
unexposed individuals.

562
00:35:17,510 --> 00:35:21,350
The characteristic lesion
is called a gong focus

563
00:35:21,350 --> 00:35:25,970
and represents an area of
central necrosis. However,

564
00:35:26,350 --> 00:35:30,570
mycobacteria might be identified
and these microorganisms

565
00:35:30,570 --> 00:35:34,050
will drain to nearby lymph
nodes which will also

566
00:35:34,050 --> 00:35:37,270
caseate. In other words,
they will become necrotic.

567
00:35:37,630 --> 00:35:41,290
In this setting, the lung
lesion and its associated

568
00:35:41,290 --> 00:35:46,170
lymph node represent the
so-called gong complex.

569
00:35:46,450 --> 00:35:49,450
The infection can be
anywhere in the lung

570
00:35:49,450 --> 00:35:52,850
but is most commonly
seen in the lower

571
00:35:52,850 --> 00:35:56,270
lobe or anterior segment
of the upper lobe.

572
00:35:57,350 --> 00:36:01,530
Histological examination
will show necrotizing

573
00:36:01,530 --> 00:36:06,550
granuloma. A necrotizing
granuloma represents an

574
00:36:06,550 --> 00:36:09,790
accumulation of immune cells
such as macrophages and

575
00:36:09,790 --> 00:36:13,630
multinucleated giant cells
which are also known as

576
00:36:13,630 --> 00:36:18,490
lancan cells surrounded by
a ream of T lymphocytes.

577
00:36:18,670 --> 00:36:22,950
The right side
microphotograph represents

578
00:36:22,950 --> 00:36:25,850
