stained section taken

579
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:29,490
to a lung with
necrotizing granuloma.

580
00:36:30,580 --> 00:36:34,030
There is obvious an
area of necrosis, or

581
00:36:34,030 --> 00:36:37,090
more specifically caseus
necrosis, surrounded

582
00:36:37,090 --> 00:36:40,310
by elongated or
epitheloid macrophages.

583
00:36:40,650 --> 00:36:43,610
There is also a
thick lymphocytic

584
00:36:43,610 --> 00:36:46,110
infiltrate and
occasional plasma cells.

585
00:36:46,690 --> 00:36:51,490
The presence of plasma
cells in this setting it's

586
00:36:51,490 --> 00:36:56,030
a sign of mycobacterium
tuberculosis infection

587
00:36:58,060 --> 00:37:03,130
identification of mycobacterium
tuberculosis can be done

588
00:37:03,130 --> 00:37:06,430
by microscopic evaluation
of sputum this begins

589
00:37:06,430 --> 00:37:10,610
by making a smear the sputum
is pressed and applied

590
00:37:10,610 --> 00:37:14,490
uniformly on the slide
then the smeared slides are

591
