heat fixed before staining
one of the most common

592
00:37:18,370 --> 00:37:21,290
methods to visualize
mycobacterial tuberculosis

593
00:37:21,290 --> 00:37:25,450
under a microscope is
represented by the carbofruxin

594
00:37:25,450 --> 00:37:31,170
or ziel nielsen method
mycobacteria acid fast and

595
00:37:31,170 --> 00:37:33,890
they would retain stain
when treated with acid and

596
00:37:33,890 --> 00:37:37,870
alcohol because of waxy
cell made of mycolic acid

597
00:37:38,610 --> 00:37:40,990
however the gold standard for

598
00:37:40,990 --> 00:37:45,170
diagnosis is represented
by the culture

599
00:37:46,290 --> 00:37:49,650
This image, inserted on
this slide, represents

600
00:37:49,650 --> 00:37:52,600
sputum from a patient
with a mycobacterium

601
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:54,730
tuberculosis
infection of the lung.

602
00:37:54,730 --> 00:37:58,890
The bacilli appear as a
red-pinkish cylindrical

603
00:37:58,890 --> 00:38:02,830
structure admixed with
degenerated epithelial cells.

604
00:38:03,990 --> 00:38:06,610
As previously
mentioned, we will not

605
00:38:06,610 --> 00:38:09,090
debate the lung
infection caused by

606
00:38:09,090 --> 00:38:12,310
mycobacterium
tuberculosis in detail.

607
00:38:12,590 --> 00:38:13,350
However,

608
00:38:13,530 --> 00:38:15,790
I would like to
stress that all the

609
00:38:15,790 --> 00:38:18,130
pathological changes
seen in a patient

610
00:38:18,550 --> 00:38:21,150
with mycobacterial
tuberculosis infection

611
00:38:21,150 --> 00:38:25,870
represent the outcome
of a TH1 response.

612
00:38:26,210 --> 00:38:29,410
TH1 refers to the immunological

613
00:38:29,410 --> 00:38:32,770
activation of a
subset of lymphocytes.

614
00:38:33,530 --> 00:38:36,730
I have to say that there
are two main types of

615
00:38:36,730 --> 00:38:39,170
lymphocytes distinguished
by the presence of

616
00:38:39,170 --> 00:38:43,730
certain surface molecules
known as CD4 and CD8.

617
00:38:44,370 --> 00:38:48,630
T-lymphocytes expressing
CD4 are known as

618
00:38:48,630 --> 00:38:53,890
helper T cells. This
subset of CD4 helper T

619
00:38:53,890 --> 00:38:58,890
-lymphocytes is further
subdivided into Th1 and

620
00:38:58,890 --> 00:39:02,670
Th2, and the cytokines
they produce are known

621
00:39:02,670 --> 00:39:06,870
as Th1-type cytokines
and Th2-type cytokines.

622
00:39:07,550 --> 00:39:13,050
Interferon gamma is the
main Th1 cytokine Interferon

623
00:39:13,050 --> 00:39:18,050
gamma generates oxidative
factors that aid intracellular

624
00:39:18,050 --> 00:39:22,330
killing of microbes in general
However, the activation

625
00:39:22,330 --> 00:39:27,550
of these CD4 helper T cells
induces also granuloma

626
00:39:27,550 --> 00:39:32,650
formation and necrosis In
these patients, Th1 leads

627
00:39:32,650 --> 00:39:36,370
to a hypersensitivity reaction
with tissue destruction

628
00:39:38,550 --> 00:39:42,070
Another type of
lung infection with

629
00:39:42,070 --> 00:39:44,630
mycobacterial
tuberculosis is secondary

630
00:39:44,630 --> 00:39:47,310
or reactivation
pulmonary tuberculosis.

631
00:39:47,470 --> 00:39:51,620
It is also known as post
-primary tuberculosis

632
00:39:51,620 --> 00:39:54,570
and is described
in 5 to 10 percent

633
00:39:54,570 --> 00:39:57,010
of patients with
primary tuberculosis.

634
00:39:57,330 --> 00:40:00,830
The lesion can occur
anywhere in the lung where

635
00:40:00,830 --> 00:40:05,490
bacteria from the primary
lesion have spread, but

636
00:40:05,490 --> 00:40:08,570
in the majority of causes
it begins at the apex

637
00:40:08,570 --> 00:40:13,610
of lung as a small focus
of less than 3 cm, which

638
00:40:13,610 --> 00:40:16,690
in some cases could
develop into a pneumonia.

639
00:40:17,430 --> 00:40:21,450
It is characterized by
the presence of a fibrotic

640
00:40:21,450 --> 00:40:26,110
