patient develops a delayed

748
00:47:01,810 --> 00:47:04,650
type hypersensitivity
reaction to the fungus.

749
00:47:04,950 --> 00:47:09,410
In western US or Mexico,
up to 80% of people

750
00:47:09,410 --> 00:47:12,010
have been infected
with this organism.

751
00:47:12,310 --> 00:47:16,690
However, only 10% of
infected individuals will

752
00:47:16,690 --> 00:47:19,790
develop lung lesions in
keeping with pneumonia.

753
00:47:20,130 --> 00:47:23,350
1% of those infected
will develop

754
00:47:23,350 --> 00:47:25,770
disseminated disease,
unfortunately.

755
00:47:26,350 --> 00:47:29,650
In terms of pathogenesis,
when these spores

756
00:47:29,650 --> 00:47:32,750
are ingested by alveolar
macrophages, they will

757
00:47:32,750 --> 00:47:36,270
block fusion of the
phagosome and lysosome,

758
00:47:36,270 --> 00:47:39,130
preventing their
destruction by macrophages.

759
00:47:39,930 --> 00:47:43,030
As you can see on the
right side microphotograph,

760
00:47:43,690 --> 00:47:48,570
these organisms present in
lung tissue as thick-walled,

761
00:47:48,570 --> 00:47:53,230
non-budding spherules filled
with small endospores.

762
00:47:57,630 --> 00:48:01,610
Pneumonia and the
immunocompromised host. In general,

763
00:48:01,610 --> 00:48:04,090
the development of a
pulmonary infiltrate even

764
00:48:04,090 --> 00:48:07,850
without signs of infection,
such as fever, is a common

765
00:48:07,850 --> 00:48:11,470
but serious complication in
patients with a depressed

766
00:48:11,470 --> 00:48:14,490
or suppressed immune
system defense mechanism.

767
00:48:14,850 --> 00:48:18,310
In this category, we also
include patients that

768
00:48:18,310 --> 00:48:21,850
are receiving immunosuppressants
after organ or

769
00:48:21,850 --> 00:48:25,130
hematopoietic stem cell
transplants and those

770
00:48:25,130 --> 00:48:28,490
receiving chemotherapy
for cancer or irradiation.

771
00:48:28,890 --> 00:48:32,130
All these patients may
develop pneumonia after

772
00:48:32,130 --> 00:48:35,810
respiratory infections with
any of the etiological agents

773
00:48:35,810 --> 00:48:39,490
mentioned so far, but
also after infection with

774
00:48:39,490 --> 00:48:43,010
so-called opportunistic
infectious agents, which

775
00:48:43,010 --> 00:48:46,890
rarely induce any pathology
in healthy individuals.

776
00:48:48,750 --> 00:48:50,770
Please note that mortality

777
00:48:50,770 --> 00:48:52,950
in these cases is very high.

778
00:48:53,530 --> 00:48:57,350
The left side table lists
some of the opportunistic

779
00:48:57,350 --> 00:49:00,950
agents according to their
prevalence and whether they

780
00:49:00,950 --> 00:49:05,110
can cause local or diffuse
pulmonary infiltrates. The

781
00:49:05,110 --> 00:49:08,450
differential diagnosis of
those infiltrates include

782
00:49:08,450 --> 00:49:12,350
drug reactions and involvement
of the lung bite tumors.

783
00:49:16,570 --> 00:49:20,730
Pulmonary infections
in HIV patients. They

784
00:49:20,730 --> 00:49:23,370
represent about 30
to 40 percent of

785
00:49:23,370 --> 00:49:26,990
hospitalizations in
HIV-infected patients.

786
00:49:27,430 --> 00:49:31,610
Despite the use of potent
antiretroviral agents,

787
00:49:31,610 --> 00:49:35,830
pulmonary infections in HIV
patients can be challenging.

788
00:49:36,830 --> 00:49:39,670
Streptococcus
pneumoniae, Staphoreus,

789
00:49:39,850 --> 00:49:42,650
Haemophilus influenzae,
and Gram-negative

790
00:49:42,650 --> 00:49:45,310
Rol, which are common
usual pathogens,

791
00:49:45,310 --> 00:49:47,310
may cause serious forms of

792
00:49:47,310 --> 00:49:49,990
pulmonary disease
in these people.

793
00:49:50,610 --> 00:49:54,370
Bacteremia is quite
common in HIV patients.

794
00:49:54,700 --> 00:49:58,550
Please note that
CD4-positive T-cells

795
00:49:58,840 --> 00:50:00,730
would determine the risk of

796
00:50:00,730 --> 00:50:03,930
infection with
specific organisms.

797
00:50:05,150 --> 00:50:08,930
Bacterial and mycobacterium
tuberculosis infections

798
00:50:08,930 --> 00:50:12,930
are seen at CD4 counts
of more than 200

799
00:50:12,930 --> 00:50:17,310
cells per cubic millimeter,
while pneumocystis

800
00:50:17,310 --> 00:50:22,010
pneumonia is described in
patients with CD4 counts

801
00:50:22,010 --> 00:50:24,970
of less than 200 cells
per cubic millimeter.

802
00:50:25,850 --> 00:50:30,270
Also, CMV and fungal
infections are seen

803
00:50:30,270 --> 00:50:34,010
in HIV patients at
counts of less than 50

804
00:50:34,010 --> 00:50:37,130
CD4-positive cells
per cubic millimeter.

805
00:50:37,710 --> 00:50:39,030
Anyway,

806
00:50:39,290 --> 00:50:42,230
not all pulmonary
infiltrates in HIV-infected

807
00:50:42,230 --> 00:50:45,930
individuals represent
infections. This is

808
00:50:45,930 --> 00:50:49,930
very important as
Kaposi's sarcoma, non

809
00:50:49,930 --> 00:50:53,390
-Hodgkin lymphoma, and lung
cancer in HIV patients

810
00:50:53,390 --> 00:50:56,330
might present with
pulmonary infiltrates.

811
00:50:58,880 --> 00:51:01,450
Now, at the end of this
lecture, I would like

812
00:51:01,450 --> 00:51:04,030
to discuss very briefly
only the morphological

813
00:51:04,030 --> 00:51:08,190
changes of pneumonia
caused by pneumocystis,

814
00:51:08,190 --> 00:51:11,810
CMV, and cryptococcus
in HIV patients.

815
00:51:13,030 --> 00:51:15,770
Neumocystis carinii
is the etiologic

816
00:51:15,770 --> 00:51:18,450
agent for pneumocystic
pneumonia.

817
00:51:19,450 --> 00:51:24,270
Neumocystis is an
extracellular pathogen which

818
00:51:24,270 --> 00:51:27,210
determines an interstitial
plasma cell pneumonia.

819
00:51:27,490 --> 00:51:31,510
The most important morphological
elements are seen on

820
00:51:31,510 --> 00:51:36,270
these microphotographs of
two hematoxylineosin stained

821
00:51:36,270 --> 00:51:41,030
lung sections which reveal
a foamy alveolar exudate,

822
00:51:41,050 --> 00:51:43,890
a mononuclear interstitial
infiltrate including

823
00:51:43,890 --> 00:51:48,190
plasma cells, and a mild
thickening of alveolar septa.

824
00:51:51,850 --> 00:51:56,270
Cytomegalovirus, CMV,
produces specific cellular

825
00:51:56,270 --> 00:51:58,990
changes in patients
with lung infection.

826
00:51:59,270 --> 00:52:03,050
On tissue examination,
we see large giant

827
00:52:03,050 --> 00:52:05,990
or cytomegalic cells
with large nuclei,

828
00:52:06,590 --> 00:52:08,890
and purple
intranuclear inclusions

829
00:52:08,890 --> 00:52:10,790
surrounded by a clear halo.

830
00:52:14,590 --> 00:52:17,250
Cryptococcus
neoformans is another

831
00:52:17,250 --> 00:52:19,710
cause of pneumonia
in HIV patients.

832
00:52:21,030 --> 00:52:24,710
Cryptococcus is an
encapsulated yeast and as shown

833
00:52:24,710 --> 00:52:27,970
here in these micro
photographs, can be identified

834
00:52:27,970 --> 00:52:31,230
in hematoxylin eosin
stained sections by its

835
00:52:31,230 --> 00:52:35,070
clear capsule which surrounds
a pale blue nucleus.

836
00:52:35,760 --> 00:52:37,670
Thank you very much
for your attention

837
00:52:37,670 --> 00:52:39,590
and please let me
know if you have

838
00:52:39,590 --> 00:52:41,790
any questions related
to this material.